  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Nevada totaled $2.6B in FY2026 to date. The state saw 18,427 awards with an average award size of $142K. Obligations fell 34.2% year over year. By fiscal year, Nevada moved from $3.1B in FY21 to $4B in FY24 and FY25, then to $2.6B in FY26. The Department of Energy and the Department of Defense are the largest buyers, at $966M and $920M respectively, followed by the General Services Administration at $487M. Top vendors in the state include MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC at $913M and FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC at $422M. The largest industry by obligations is Facilities Support Services at $988M, with Engineering Services at $429M and Automobile Manufacturing at $422M rounding out the top three. This snapshot covers fiscal year to date totals and reflects partial current-year obligations. Use these figures as a concise picture of who is buying, who is being paid, and which industries dominate Nevada federal contracting activity so far in FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to federal contracting in Nevada this year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 34.2% year over year. Total obligations for FY2026 to date are $2.6B, down from $4B in FY25. The number of awards is 18,427 and the average award size is $142K. That combination shows lower total spend while award activity and average size provide additional context for how dollars are flowing."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is the spending concentrated in Nevada federal contracts?",
        "body": "Spending is concentrated in a few agencies and industries. The Department of Energy and the Department of Defense lead buying with $966M and $920M respectively, and Facilities Support Services accounts for $988M of obligations. Major vendors reflect that concentration, with MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC at $913M and FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC at $422M. Several other industries and contractors receive meaningful shares but at lower absolute levels."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Nevada?",
      "a": "Nevada received $2.6B in federal contract obligations year to date. There were 18,427 awards and the average award size was $142K. Obligations fell 34.2% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows $3.1B in FY21, $3.3B in FY22, $3.7B in FY23, $4B in FY24, and $4B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Nevada?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy and the Department of Defense award the most contracts in Nevada. The Department of Energy obligated $966M and the Department of Defense obligated $920M in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration follows at $487M, with other agencies like the Department of Veterans Affairs at $79.8M and the Department of the Interior at $57.6M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Nevada?",
      "a": "The largest federal contractors in Nevada are MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC and FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC. MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC received $913M and FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC received $422M in FY2026 to date. Other top vendors include JT4 LLC at $297M and SIERRA NEVADA COMPANY, LLC at $216M."
